{"Negative offset vulnerability in OptimizedCursorPaginator allows negative offsets when enable_advanced_features is True, bypassing normal boundary checks. Negative list slicing in Python can expose unintended data and bypass pagination logic": 0.9251086711883545, "Missing null check on organization_context.member - accessing .has_global_access on None will cause AttributeError for users without organization membership including superusers viewing organizations they're not members of": 0.8083271384239197, "Authorization uses overly permissive 'or' condition where any member with global_access can enable advanced features including negative offset pagination": 0.6449762582778931, "Redis data structure changed from SET to ZSET without migration strategy - existing SET data will not be readable by new ZSET operations, potentially causing data loss or errors": 0.9340565800666809, "Django QuerySets do not support negative indexing - the code claims Django ORM handles negative slicing automatically but this is false, will cause TypeError or force full queryset evaluation": 0.9596120715141296, "Removed span count validation (max_segment_spans check) from _load_segment_data() reduces defensive programming and could hide Lua script eviction failures": 0.7406249046325684, "Lua script redirect depth limit reduced from 10000 to 1000 without monitoring metrics to detect when segment trees are being truncated": 0.7181100845336914}